+    <section class="journal" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
+      <h2 id="journal-title">Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <p class="journal-byline">Notes from the roastery on how our beans find their way to your cup</p>
+
+      <div class="journal-body" id="journal-text">
+        <p>Every bag of coffee we roast starts with a relationship, not a purchase order. Long before a single bean
+          reaches our roaster, our sourcing team spends months each year traveling to growing regions in Ethiopia,
+          Colombia, Guatemala, and Sumatra. We walk the farms, meet the families who tend them, and taste alongside
+          the people who know these hillsides best. Most of the producers we buy from today are partners we have
+          worked with for five years or more, and several have been with us since we opened our doors.</p>
+        <p>We buy through direct trade wherever we can, which means we negotiate prices face to face rather than
+          through commodity exchanges. On average, we pay our partner farms well above the Fairtrade minimum, and we
+          publish what we pay on every bag. Paying more is not charity; it is an investment. Farmers who earn a
+          stable living can afford to replant aging trees, build better drying beds, and hire pickers who select only
+          ripe, deep-red cherries. That care shows up directly in the cup.</p>
+        <p>Quality control begins at origin. Before any contract is signed, we cup samples from each lot on site and
+          again when pre-shipment samples arrive at our roastery. We score every coffee for sweetness, acidity, body,
+          and clarity, and we only purchase lots that score 85 points or higher on the specialty scale. When a harvest
+          falls short, we tell our partners why and work with them on processing changes for the following season
+          instead of simply walking away.</p>
+        <p>Sustainability guides how we choose which farms to work with. We prioritize shade-grown coffee, which
+          protects bird habitats and keeps soil healthy, and we favor producers who use water-saving processing
+          methods. Green coffee travels to us by sea in grain-pro bags that preserve freshness without refrigeration,
+          and we offset the emissions from every shipment. Once it arrives, we roast in small batches of no more than
+          thirty pounds so our roasters can adjust each profile by hand.</p>
+        <p>Finally, freshness is non-negotiable. We roast to order several times a week and never sell coffee more than
+          fourteen days past its roast date. Any beans that age past that window are donated to local shelters or
+          composted in our community garden. From the farm to your morning cup, every step is designed to honor the
+          work of the people who grew it.</p>
+      </div>
+
